# React/UI conventions

- Follow **`docs/DESIGN.md`** for tokens, card radius, shadows, typography, and AI (Cora) patterns before writing UI.
- Prefer **function components** and local state via React hooks.
- Reuse UI primitives in `src/components/ui/*` (e.g. `Button`, `Dialog`, `Card`, `Toaster`, `TooltipProvider`) instead of rolling custom ones.
- Use Tailwind utility classes; when composing class strings use `cn` from `@/lib/utils` if available in the file’s area.
- Card shells: prefer `<Card>` or `ds-card` / `ds-card-hover` from `globals.css` over ad-hoc `rounded-lg` panels.
- Keep components presentational where possible; move side effects / data sync into hooks or store helpers.

## Accessibility & UX

- Interactive elements must have **`type="button"`** for non-submit buttons and meaningful **`aria-*`** / `alt` text.
- Icon-only buttons need **`aria-label`**; mobile touch targets ≥ 44×44px.
- Prefer `NavLink` active styling patterns already used in `src/pages/account/Account.tsx`.
- Icons: **`lucide-react` only** (no new icon packs). OpenCampus CTAs use `bg-ocid-blue` per DESIGN.md §11.
